  "rules": [
   "Word order is Subject-Object-Verb. The verb comes last in the clause, unlike English Subject-Verb-Object.",
   "Relators FOLLOW their noun as postpositions; they are never placed before it like English prepositions. 'in the house' is house + inside.",
   "Grammatical case is marked by a suffix glued onto the end of the noun or pronoun, not by a separate word.",
   "There are no articles. Nothing corresponds to English 'a', 'an' or 'the'.",
   "Adjectives and other modifiers come before the noun they modify.",
   "A question is formed with a question word plus normal word order; the subject and verb are not inverted the way English inverts them.",
   "Negation is expressed with a dedicated negative word or verb form, not by inserting an equivalent of English 'do not'."
  ],
